\] Next, we calculate the value inside the parentheses: \[
\frac{125 + 68 - 81}{18} = \frac{112}{18} = \frac{56}{9}
\] Now we square this value: \[
\left( \frac{56}{9} \right)^2 = \frac{3136}{81}
\] Then we subtract this from the square of the first radius: \[
125 - \frac{3136}{81} = \frac{10125 - 3136}{81} = \frac{6989}{81}
